{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310531,"nonce":"3oU45Xp8O1Prjgpm7EYjkAfxuOU=","title":"OPEN codegen panic: an Array.sort comparator closure that uses one of its params as an INDEX into another array crashes the LLVM JIT ...","message":"CRASHES — comparator param used as an array index:\n```haxe\nvar scores = [3.0, 1.0, 2.0];\nvar order = [0, 1, 2];\norder.sort(function(a, b):Int {\n    var d = scores[b] - scores[a]; // b/a used as INDEX into `scores`\n    return (d \u003e 0) ? 1 : (d \u003c 0 ? -1 : 0);\n});\n```\n→ `thread 'main' panicked at compiler/src/codegen/llvm_jit_backend.rs:3115:43: Found\nPointerValue(...) but expected the IntValue variant`.\n\nWORKS — comparator params compared arithmetically (no array index):\n```haxe\norder.sort(function(a, b):Int { return a - b; }); // prints sorted 1 2 3\n```\n\n`llvm_jit_backend.rs:~3101` lowers GEP indices: `val.into_int_value()` at 3115 assumes the index\nregister is an int. Array.sort passes each element to the comparator BOXED (as an Any/pointer slot);\nthe comparator param `a`/`b` therefore holds a pointer. Used in arithmetic it gets unboxed first, but\nused directly as `scores[b]` the GEP-index path receives the raw pointer → `into_int_value()` panics.\nLikely fix: unbox/int-coerce a boxed comparator param before it feeds an array-index GEP (either at\nthe sort-comparator param binding, or defensively in the GEP-index lowering when the value is a\npointer that should be an integer index). NOT yet attempted — orthogonal to BERT; surfaced by the\nvector-search demo. Related boxing-of-primitive issues: [[bugs_nue_metaint_unbox_raw_enum_payload]].\n\n`nue/examples/vector-search/Main.hx` selects top-k by manual O(n·k) max-scan over a `used[]` mask\ninstead of `Array.sort` with a comparator — cheaper for k≪n anyway and avoids this path entirely.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_array_sort_comparator_param_gep` on 2026-10-18.